            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A display panel and a display apparatus. The display panel comprises: a first display region (R1);a second display region (R2), at least located on a side of the first display region (R1);a plurality of sub-pixels, located in the first display region (R1) and the second display region (R2), a density of the sub-pixels in the first display region (R1) being less than a density of the sub-pixels in the second display region (R2), and each of the plurality of the sub-pixel comprising a pixel circuit (10);a plurality of pixel groups (P1), located in the first display region (R1), at least one of the plurality of pixel groups (P1) comprising at least two sub-pixels; and a first power line (311), configured to provide a first voltage signal (ELVDD) to the pixel circuit (10), the first power line (311) extends to the first display region (R1) from the second display region (R2);a plurality of data lines (313), configured to be connected to the plurality of pixel groups (P1), to provide a data signal to the plurality of pixel groups (P1),wherein between adjacent pixel groups (P1) of the plurality of pixel groups (P1), an orthogonal projection on the substrate (BS) of a partial segment of at least one of the plurality of data lines (313) falls within an orthogonal projection on the substrate (BS) of the first power line (311). By means of the display panel, the mesh structure of a first power line can be more stable, and the voltage drop on the first power line is reduced, such that the brightness uniformity of the display panel is better.</p>
            </abstract>
